A||||3||mshill||Rear Anti-swaybar: Oh my...||||14||
Z||000000||mshill||03-30-2001||03:52 AM||||I just got finished installing a stock front anti-swaybar on the rearend of my 86SE and I cannot believe the difference that it makes.  Now the car actually handles almost as good as it looks.<P>I followed the instructions from some website that suggested that you use the 3 1/2 inch AddCo endlinks.  I finished mine up and I think the bar is too low.  I think I am going to shorten the andlinks about 1 1/2 inches. so they don't hang down so low.<P>I loved to drive tha car before, now I just won't want to stop.||||reg||14
Z||000001||rockcrawl||03-30-2001||07:56 AM||||I did the same thing on my '87 GT and wow what a difference. It seems to oversteer a little now. For endlinks I just used bushings and washers, no spacers.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||03-30-2001||08:40 AM||||I think I read on the Forum somewhere that the ideal setup is to have the bar ends level with the ground.||||reg||1
Z||000003||danny boy||03-30-2001||06:19 PM|||| My 1" bar install should be done by tomorrow. Since I have a whole 4" of ground clearance I'm setting it inside the frame rails Ala Citation. When I'm done I'll tell everyone how I did it(unless it doesn't work.)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
